course: dictionary
lesson: 721
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «When its moss dries out, a tardigrade curls into a dry little barrel called a tun.» Here barrel means a small round shape, because the tardigrade curls up into a ball, not into a wooden container.
explain: Barrel can also be a noun for the long tube of a gun, or a verb. «Big cats play with balls, ropes and barrels» tells you the barrels are round objects that cats can play with, like toys.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one. If not, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: A barrel is a big round container with a flat top and bottom, often made of wood or metal, used to hold liquids or goods.
fact: A barrel is also the long tube of a gun, where the bullet comes out.
fact: A barrel can be an amount: for oil, it is about 159 litres.
fact: To barrel along means to move very fast and without control.
fact: «A barrel of laughs» means lots of fun, and «scrape the bottom of the barrel» means use the worst of what is left.
exercise: «When its moss dries out, a tardigrade curls into a dry little barrel.» What shape is the barrel in this sentence? | A fast moving car | *A small round shape, like a ball | A long thin tube | A cold drink
exercise: Lily says, «The bus began to barrel along the motorway.» What does barrel along mean? | *To move very fast and without control | To stop and rest for a while | To sleep softly in a corner | To sing very loudly
exercise: The water barrel by the shed fills up when it rains. What is a water barrel? | *A big round container for water | A tall tree | A tube for a bullet | A kind of bird
test: The old ship carried water, apples and fish in wooden barrels. What were the barrels used for? | *To hold liquids and goods | To show feelings | To fire bullets | To keep the sailors warm
test: «We were in a hard spot, so we were over a barrel.» What does over a barrel mean? | Lying on top of a barrel | Having a great time | Moving very fast | *In a hard position
exam: «The soldier cleaned the barrel of his gun.» Which meaning of barrel fits this sentence? | *The long tube of a gun | A big round container | An amount of oil | To move very fast and without control
